{"lines": ["Every autumn, birds fall out of the dark sky over one village in India. Nobody agrees why.", "Jatinga, Assam. A ridge-top village, on foggy, moonless nights, between six and nine-thirty.", "Birds drop toward the village lights. Kingfishers, herons, pigeons. Young ones, mostly.", "Locals feared a curse. In the 1960s, the world heard of it, and the press called it bird suicide.", "One zoologist blamed magnetic energy in the ridge. Another blamed the wind and fog.", "But here's the twist. Birds caught there recovered within hours, and flew away. They weren't trying to die.", "A five-year study found young migrants steering by the moon. No moon, and any light can pull them in.", "And on those nights, villagers waited with torches and bamboo poles.", "So, mass suicide, or a trap? Tell me below."], "words": [["Every", 0.0, 0.2], ["autumn,", 0.2, 0.54], ["birds", 0.94, 1.22], ["fall", 1.22, 1.56], ["out", 1.56, 1.76], ["of", 1.76, 1.86], ["the", 1.86, 1.94], ["dark", 1.94, 2.14], ["sky", 2.14, 2.48], ["over", 2.48, 2.86], ["one", 2.86, 3.1], ["village", 3.1, 3.36], ["in", 3.36, 3.74], ["India.", 3.74, 4.06], ["Nobody", 4.66, 5.08], ["agrees", 5.08, 5.6], ["why.", 5.6, 6.0], ["Jatinga,", 6.602, 7.0], ["Assam.", 7.32, 7.72], ["A", 8.42, 8.46], ["ridge-top", 8.46, 8.98], ["village,", 8.98, 9.32], ["on", 9.32, 9.7], ["foggy,", 9.7, 10.28], ["moonless", 10.46, 10.76], ["nights,", 10.76, 11.02], ["between", 11.44, 11.64], ["six", 11.64, 11.98], ["and", 11.98, 12.28], ["nine-thirty.", 12.28, 12.84], ["Birds", 13.347, 13.56], ["drop", 13.56, 13.84], ["toward", 13.84, 14.22], ["the", 14.22, 14.42], ["village", 14.42, 14.62], ["lights.", 14.62, 14.9], ["Kingfishers,", 15.7, 15.9], ["herons,", 16.38, 16.68], ["pigeons.", 16.9, 17.34], ["Young", 17.86, 18.06], ["ones,", 18.06, 18.34], ["mostly.", 18.34, 18.8], ["Locals", 19.443, 19.88], ["feared", 19.88, 20.2], ["a", 20.2, 20.4], ["curse.", 20.4, 20.66], ["In", 21.46, 21.56], ["the", 21.56, 21.62], ["1960s,", 21.62, 23.16]